# Neo Learn String parameters (docs/specs/neo-learn.md, neo-learn-controls.md A1 and A2.13). The order is permanent: songs and
# presets store values by position. The 12 controls are the six core ones, then the six global ones (Attack, Decay, Sustain, Release,
# Unison / Spread, Output). Each has a snake_case id, and the Explain text (How, Sound; the description is the How line).
# Regenerate: python3 tools/gen-machine-params.py Machines/NeoLearnString
namespace NeoBuzz.LearnString
class NeoLearnStringMachine
tracks 16
summary Teaching string synth: one Dye Essence patch driven by 12 controls. A Karplus-Strong string: a delay line plucked with a burst of noise (its hardness and where on the string), a loop that loses treble (damping) and a little level each time round (a decay time of 0.05 to 20 s at any note), a dispersion all-pass that stiffens it toward a piano wire or a chime, and sympathetic strings an octave and a fifth up, with an ADSR, unison and an output gain. Every control says what it does and what you will hear. Use it for harps, guitars, harpsichords, kotos, pianos and bells, or to learn how plucked-string synthesis works.

group Core
PickPosition     "Pick Position" 0 1000 300 pct
    id pluck_position
    how Pre-filters the initial excitation impulse with a comb notch corresponding to where the string is plucked (0% Bridge -> 100% Center).
    sound Plucking near the bridge sounds sharp, nasal, and harpsichord-like; plucking near the center sounds round and hollow.
StringDamping    "String Damping" 0 1000 350 pct
    id string_damping
    how Adjusts the cutoff of the one-pole low-pass filter inside the delay feedback loop.
    sound Low damping lets bright metallic harmonics ring out; high damping absorbs treble rapidly like a nylon or palm-muted guitar.
PickHardness     "Pick Hardness" 0 1000 500 pct
    id pick_hardness
    how Controls the duration and high-frequency content of the noise/impulse burst injected into the delay line at note-on.
    sound Morphs the initial attack from a soft flesh thumb brush to a stiff nylon plectrum or hard metal hammer.
StringDecay      "Decay Time" 0 1000 683 time 0.05 20
    id string_decay
    how Sets the loop gain per cycle from the pitch, so the string falls 60 dB in this time at any note (T60).
    sound Controls how long the string sustains after being plucked, from tight staccato ticks to long harp rings.
Dispersion       "Stiffness" 0 1000 80 pct
    id dispersion
    how Increases the all-pass filter coefficient inside the feedback loop so high frequencies travel faster than low frequencies.
    sound Pushes the string physics from an ideal flexible guitar string into a stiff piano wire, chime, or metallic bell.
SympatheticRes   "Sympathetic" 0 1000 150 pct
    id sympathetic_res
    how Bleeds a fraction of the plucked string's energy into a bank of unplucked octaves and fifths delay lines.
    sound Adds the lush, resonant halo of unplayed strings vibrating sympathetically across a harp, sitar, or acoustic guitar body.

group Global
EnvAttack        "Attack" 0 1000 150 time 0.0005 5
    id env_attack
    how Sets the time required for the note's amplitude (and routed envelope modulation) to ramp from silence to full peak after a note-on trigger.
    sound Low values create immediate, percussive plucks; high values produce slow, swelling pads.
EnvDecay         "Decay" 0 1000 812 time 0.005 8
    id env_decay
    how Controls how long it takes for the signal to drop from peak level down to the sustain level while a key remains held.
    sound Short decay makes notes snappy and tight; longer decay gives a gradual piano- or bell-like fade.
EnvSustain       "Sustain" 0 1000 1000 pct
    id env_sustain
    how Defines the steady-state volume level maintained for as long as a note is held after the Attack and Decay stages complete.
    sound At 0% the synth behaves like a plucked or struck instrument; at 100% it holds full organ-like volume.
EnvRelease       "Release" 0 1000 577 time 0.005 10
    id env_release
    how Sets the time required for the sound to fade from its current level to complete silence after the note is released.
    sound Short release stops notes abruptly; long release leaves an ambient tail that blends chords together.
UnisonDetune     "Unison / Spread" 0 1000 0 pct
    id unison_detune
    how 0% plays one voice per note; above 0% each note plays 5 detuned, stereo-spread voices (3 in Additive, Granular and Spectral), with detune (up to ±50 cents) and width growing with the value.
    sound Thickens thin waveforms into wide, chorus-like stereo leads and pads.
OutputGain       "Output" 0 1000 700 db -36 12
    id output_gain
    how Sets the level after synthesis. There is no limiter (NeoBuzz mixes in floating point); a clip light shows when the output passes 0 dBFS.
    sound Controls overall loudness; keep the clip light dark when the next machine expects levels at or below 0 dBFS.

# What the machine measures (NeoLearnStringMachine.Readings, machine_readings): the output after Output, in dBFS.
reading rms_db dB | The output's RMS over about half a second (-inf: silence)
reading peak_db dB | The output's peak, falling 20 dB a second (-inf: silence)
reading active_voices notes | Notes sounding now (unison voices belong to their note)
